{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && sed -n '1,260p' resources.md\"","aggregated_output":"/workspaces/reasoning-trace-robustnes-318e-codex\n# Resources Catalog\n\n## Summary\nThis document catalogs all resources gathered for the project on reasoning trace length and OOD robustness.\n\n### Search Strategy\n- Attempted `paper-finder` diligent mode first; service timed out in this run.\n- Fallback: manual arXiv + Semantic Scholar API search with relevance filtering.\n- Downloaded foundational and recent papers covering CoT, process supervision, OOD analysis, and test-time compute.\n\n### Selection Criteria\n- Direct relevance to trace length, trace selection, or OOD robustness.\n- Inclusion of both foundational baselines and 2025 updates.\n- Preference for papers with available code/data or executable evaluation setup.\n\n## Papers\nTotal papers downloaded: 16\n\n| Title | Authors | Year | File | Key Info |\n|-------|---------|------|------|----------|\n| Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in LLMs | Wei et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2201.11903v6_chain_of_thought_prompting_elicits_reasoning_in_la.pdf | Foundational CoT baseline |\n| Self-Consistency Improves CoT Reasoning | Wang et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2203.11171v4_self_consistency_improves_chain_of_thought_reasoni.pdf | Multi-trace vote baseline |\n| Tree of Thoughts | Yao et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.10601v2_tree_of_thoughts_deliberate_problem_solving_with_l.pdf | Search-based reasoning |\n| Let’s Verify Step by Step | Lightman et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.20050v1_let_s_verify_step_by_step.pdf | PRM vs ORM; PRM800K |\n| Chain-of-Thought Hub | Fu et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.17306v1_chain_of_thought_hub_a_continuous_effort_to_measur.pdf | Benchmark suite |\n| Math-Shepherd | Wang et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2312.08935v3_math_shepherd_verify_and_reinforce_llms_step_by_st.pdf | Auto process reward |\n| Contrastive CoT Prompting | Chia et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2311.09277v1_contrastive_chain_of_thought_prompting.pdf | Positive/negative traces |\n| GRACE | Khalifa et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.14934v3_grace_discriminator_guided_chain_of_thought_reason.pdf | Discriminator-guided decoding |\n| OCEAN | Wu et al. | 2024 | papers/2024_2410.23703v1_ocean_offline_chain_of_thought_evaluation_and_alig.pdf | Offline CoT evaluator |\n| Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning OOD | Bao et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2207.14000v4_multi_step_deductive_reasoning_over_natural_langua.pdf | Explicit OOD reasoning setup |\n| CoT as Policy Improvement | Zhang & Parkes | 2023 | papers/2023_2309.08589v2_chain_of_thought_reasoning_is_a_policy_improvement.pdf | Theoretical framing |\n| Buffer of Thoughts | Yang et al. | 2024 | papers/2024_2406.04271v2_buffer_of_thoughts_thought_augmented_reasoning_wit.pdf | Thought template memory |\n| Is CoT a Mirage? | Zhao et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2508.01191v4_is_chain_of_thought_reasoning_of_llms_a_mirage_a_d.pdf | Distribution-lens failures |\n| Slim-SC | Hong et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2509.13990v1_slim_sc_thought_pruning_for_efficient_scaling_with.pdf | Pruned self-consistency |\n| Sleep-time Compute | Lin et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2504.13171v1_sleep_time_compute_beyond_inference_scaling_at_tes.pdf | Offline compute strategy |\n| Long CoT Survey | Chen et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2503.09567v5_towards_reasoning_era_a_survey_of_long_chain_of_th.pdf | State-of-field survey |\n\nSee `papers/README.md` for detailed descriptions.\n\n## Datasets\nTotal datasets downloaded: 6\n\n| Name | Source | Size | Task | Location | Notes |\n|------|--------|------|------|----------|-------|\n| GSM8K | Hugging Face `gsm8k/main` | 7,473 train / 1,319 test | math reasoning | datasets/gsm8k_main/ | Baseline CoT benchmark |\n| MATH-500 | Hugging Face `HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500` | 500 test | hard math reasoning | datasets/math500/ | Hard-set robustness |\n| ARC-Challenge | Hugging Face `allenai/ai2_arc` | 1,119/299/1,172 | science QA reasoning | datasets/ai2_arc_challenge/ | Domain shift |\n| BBH: multistep_arithmetic_two | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | symbolic/multi-step | datasets/bbh_multistep_arithmetic_two/ | OOD-style stress test |\n| BBH: logical_deduction_three_objects | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | logical reasoning | datasets/bbh_logical_deduction_three_objects/ | Trace-quality sensitive |\n| BBH: date_understanding | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | temporal reasoning | datasets/bbh_date_understanding/ | Diverse reasoning type |\n\nSee `datasets/README.md` for download/loading instructions.\n\n## Code Repositories\nTotal repositories cloned: 3\n\n| Name | URL | Purpose | Location | Notes |\n|------|-----|---------|----------|-------|\n| chain-of-thought-hub | https://github.com/FranxYao/chain-of-thought-hub | benchmark scripts/templates | code/chain-of-thought-hub/ | includes BBH, GSM8K, MMLU runners |\n| tree-of-thought-llm | https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm | deliberate search inference | code/tree-of-thought-llm/ | ToT + BFS baseline |\n| prm800k | https://github.com/openai/prm800k | process supervision dataset + eval | code/prm800k/ | PRM/ORM evaluation utilities |\n\nSee `code/README.md` for details.\n\n## Resource Gathering Notes\n\n### Challenges Encountered\n- `paper-finder` service timed out, so manual API-based retrieval was used.\n- `uv add` failed because the workspace is not configured as an installable package; fallback to `uv pip install` succeeded.\n- `hendrycks/competition_math` dataset identifier was unavailable on HF; replaced with `MATH-500` plus additional BBH tasks.\n\n### Gaps and Workarounds\n- No single canonical OOD dataset for trace-length studies; combined math + science + BBH tasks and recommend adding a synthetic controlled OOD generator for final experiments.\n\n## Recommendations for Experiment Design\n\n1. **Primary datasets**: GSM8K + MATH-500 for core reasoning; BBH+ARC for distribution shift.\n2. **Baseline methods**: direct answer, fixed-length CoT, self-consistency, ToT, verifier/reranker methods.\n3. **Evaluation metrics**: ID/OOD accuracy, robustness gap, token cost, calibration/error-consistency.\n4. **Code to adapt**: use `chain-of-thought-hub` for benchmark plumbing, `tree-of-thought-llm` for adaptive search, and `prm800k` for process-supervision/verifier pipelines.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
